# Button icons

Every interactive button (`Button`, native `<button>`, and button-like controls that act as actions) **must include an icon**. Do not ship text-only or empty action buttons.

## Prefer project wrappers

- Prefer `@/components/Button` over raw `<button>` for app actions.
- Prefer icons from `@/components/icons` (`IconSave`, `IconTrash`, …). If missing, add a wrapper there or use `lucide-react` consistently with existing size defaults (usually 14–16).

## Layout

- Place the icon **before** the label (LTR). `Button` already uses `gap-2` — do not add extra spacer hacks.
- Icon-only buttons are allowed when space is tight; always set `aria-label` (and usually `title`).
- Label-only buttons are **not** allowed.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — text only
<Button variant="secondary" onClick={onSave}>저장</Button>
<button type="button" onClick={onCancel}>취소</button>

// ✅ GOOD — icon + label
<Button variant="secondary" onClick={onSave}>
  <IconSave size={14} />
  저장
</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — icon only with accessible name (+ Radix Tooltip if a hover hint is needed; never title=)
<Button variant="tertiary" onClick={onClose} aria-label="닫기">
  <IconX size={14} />
</Button>
```

## Built-in exceptions

- `ConfirmModal` / `DeleteConfirmModal` already inject cancel/confirm icons — do not pass duplicate icons for those built-in actions (see `confirm-modal` rule).
- Non-button controls (links styled as text, checkbox/switch/radio, menu item chevrons that are not the action affordance) are out of scope unless they are implemented as `<button>` / `Button` action triggers.

## When editing UI

If you touch a button that is still text-only, add an appropriate icon in the same change.
